{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 BANKING SECTOR KNOWLEDGE GRAPH ONTOLOGY Listed Companies in India \u8212- Event-Free, Analyst-Oriented (v2 \u8212- extended)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 v2 changelog: adds governance/ownership, credit ratings, and macroeconomic factors as new entity and relationship types, closing gaps identified against the v1 ontology. All v1 sections are unchanged unless noted.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab DESIGN PRINCIPLES \u8226 ? Capture persistent structural knowledge, not events or timelines. \u8226 ? Separate objective facts from analytical interpretation. \u8226 ? Use reusable, normalized entities across companies. \u8226 ? Prefer explicit, directional, semantically meaningful relationships. \u8226 ? Store metric definitions separately from company-specific metric values. \u8226 ? Preserve confidence and evidence strength for analytical knowledge.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab CORE KNOWLEDGE LAYERS\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Layer 1 \u8212- Structural Knowledge Sector, Industry, BankingSegment, Company, CorporateGroup, Product, Service, CustomerSegment, Geography, DistributionChannel, Regulator, License, Person, PromoterGroup, Shareholder, CreditRatingAgency, CreditRating.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Layer 2 \u8212- Business and Economic Knowledge BusinessModel, OperatingModel, RevenueStream, FundingSource, AssetClass, LiabilityClass, LoanSegment, DepositSegment, InvestmentClass, Capability, Technology, CompetitiveArena, Partnership, Ecosystem, Metric, MacroeconomicFactor.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Layer 3 \u8212- Analyst Knowledge Strength, Weakness, Opportunity, Threat, Risk, Dependency, Driver, CompetitiveAdvantage, StrategicPosition, Claim, Condition, Outcome.\par}
